The repos/ snapshot the recorded baselines were taken against.

Every baseline here (apt-*.names, apk-*.names, opam-*.sel, lock-*.json, and
cargo's per-goal results) is an answer about one fixed universe, so it is only
comparable against the same snapshot.  scripts/fetch-repos.sh fetches the
current head of each source and pins nothing -- it takes today's Debian
`stable` Packages, today's Alpine v3.21 APKINDEX, a --depth 1 clone of
whichever commit opam-repository and crates.io-index are on, and whatever the
npm registry serves -- so a fresh fetch will not in general reproduce these
identifiers, and a differing one means the baselines must be regenerated
rather than compared.

The tools the baselines were taken with (apt, apk, opam, cargo and rustc, npm
and node) are pinned by nix/flake.lock; run the harnesses inside `nix develop ./nix`,
which provides them.

Fetched 2026-09-10/11 with scripts/fetch-repos.sh at its defaults
(DEBIAN_SUITE=stable, DEBIAN_ARCH=amd64, ALPINE_VER=v3.21, ALPINE_ARCH=x86_64).

